// A vetted epistemology library — first principles only, no facts. A human
// curates it once; the model imports it and only supplies the concrete case.
//
// The classical analysis: "S knows that P" = justified true belief (JTB).
//   (1) P is true          — the truth condition
//   (2) S believes P       — the belief condition
//   (3) S is justified      — the justification condition
// Knowledge is their conjunction. This file states the constraints; the importing
// file writes the facts and asks the engine whether the case amounts to knowledge.

DOMAIN epistemics

// Each JTB condition is necessary: knowledge entails all three.
PREMISE knowledge_needs_truth:
    WHEN claim is_knowledge
    THEN claim is_true

PREMISE knowledge_needs_belief:
    WHEN claim is_knowledge
    THEN claim is_believed

PREMISE knowledge_needs_justification:
    WHEN claim is_knowledge
    THEN claim is_justified

// The Gettier defeater (Gettier 1963): a claim can be justified, true, AND believed
// yet fail to be knowledge when luck — not the evidence — is what makes it true.
// A "gettiered" claim is therefore NOT knowledge, however impeccable its JTB
// credentials. This one *derives* a value (non-knowledge), so it is a RULE, not a
// checked PREMISE — the importing file's `FACT claim is_gettiered` fires it.
RULE gettier_defeats_knowledge:
    WHEN claim is_gettiered
    THEN NOT claim is_knowledge
